WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.417
A moving average uses a sliding frame rather than an ever-growing frame.

00:00:04.417 --> 00:00:10.922
With two preceding rows and the current row, the calculation uses up to three ordered rows.

00:00:10.922 --> 00:00:15.992
At the beginning of the sequence, fewer than three rows may be available.

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:19.512
The frame moves forward with the current row.

00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:23.462
Running and moving calculations depend on the window frame.

00:00:23.462 --> 00:00:29.542
Defaults can be surprising, especially with duplicate ordering values or LAST_VALUE.

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:33.587
Write the frame explicitly when the intended range matters.

00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:39.008
A clear frame makes the query easier to audit and protects against subtle changes in data.
